## English Version

# The Demise of Close Friend B.C. Nagesh Is Deeply Painful

## His Last Rites Will Be Conducted With Full State Honours: DCM Dr. G. Parameshwara

**Tipatur, August 19:** Deputy Chief Minister Dr. G. Parameshwara expressed deep sorrow over the demise of former minister and his close friend B.C. Nagesh.

After paying his last respects to the mortal remains of B.C. Nagesh, Dr. Parameshwara said that his last rites would be conducted with full state honours.

He described Nagesh as a warm and friendly person who treated everyone with trust and affection. Despite being well-off, Nagesh never displayed his status and continued to help people throughout his public life.

Dr. Parameshwara recalled that Nagesh would frequently call him for advice and discussions when he was serving as a minister.

"Although I belonged to a different political party, our friendship was very deep," Dr. Parameshwara recalled.

### Memories of the 1994 Election

Dr. Parameshwara recalled that B.C. Nagesh personally visited his residence after he lost the 1994 election.

At the time, Nagesh had urged him to join the BJP and had conveyed that Ananth Kumar had sent him to persuade Dr. Parameshwara. He also spoke about L.K. Advani's proposed visit to Tumakuru and the possibility of announcing a ticket for him.

Dr. Parameshwara said he declined the proposal because the ideological positions of the two parties were different.

He recalled telling Nagesh that despite their political differences, they should remain good friends.

Their friendship continued despite their political differences, he said.

Dr. Parameshwara also recalled that whenever Nagesh travelled to Bengaluru, he would stop his car in front of his residence and visit him if he was at home.

"That was the depth of our friendship," he recalled.

Expressing grief over the loss, Dr. Parameshwara prayed for the eternal peace of B.C. Nagesh's soul and conveyed his condolences to the bereaved family.

